      "note": "SST rate file (SSTGB Technology Guide layout): COMPONENT records \u2014 each row is ONE taxing authority's own rate, typed by `level` (county, city, special_district). The rate at an address is the state rate plus EVERY applicable local record summed, and which locals apply is defined by the companion SST BOUNDARY file, which this dataset does NOT ship. States differ: inside an incorporated city Washington assigns no county record, while Kansas assigns county AND city. Do not assume the most specific record is the whole local rate, and do not sum every record for a code \u2014 without boundary data these records are a rate catalogue keyed by jurisdiction, not an address-resolvable map."
